# No SPA catch-all here any more.
#
# It used to be "/*  /index.html  200", which made every unmatched path return
# HTTP 200 carrying the homepage HTML - a soft 404. Google treats those as
# duplicate content and they are indexable, so a mistyped or spammed URL became
# a crawlable page claiming to be the site.
#
# Each real route now has its own prerendered file in dist (see
# scripts/prerender.mjs), which Cloudflare Pages serves directly. Anything with
# no matching file falls through to dist/404.html, which Pages returns with a
# real 404 status.
#
# Add genuine redirects below as "  /old-path  /new-path  301".
